# The files a Blindspot release signs and attaches (docs/designs/signed-releases.md), one per line:
# the file name, a space, then how the release gets it.
#
#   committed   the file as committed in the reviewed commit
#   built       made by bash tools/gen.sh from the reviewed commit, at release
#   unreleased  not released: a path (* matches any part of one) people never run from a release
#
# Every file people could run is named here: every tracked file, at any depth, that is executable,
# starts with #!, or ends in .sh, .bash, .zsh, .ksh, .fish, .ps1, .psm1, .psd1, .bat, .cmd,
# .command, .py, .pl, .rb, .js or .vbs, and every file tools/gen.sh builds. A pull request that
# adds one adds its line too, or says on an unreleased line, with the reason in a comment above it,
# why it is not released. bash tools/release.sh --check-list checks this, and tests/release.sh
# runs that check. A released name is letters, digits, ".", "_" and "-".
gird-check.ps1 committed
gird-check.sh committed
gird-fleet.sh committed
gird-fleet.ps1 committed
gird-intune.ps1 committed
gird-report.ps1 committed
blindspot-fleet.sh built
blindspot-fleet.ps1 built
# The test suites and their helpers: maintainers and CI run them from a checkout.
tests/* unreleased
# The maintainers' tools (gen.sh, release.sh, the review guard, strip-comments.ps1, which gen.sh
# runs to build blindspot-fleet.ps1): run from a checkout, never from a release.
tools/* unreleased
